{"computedAt":"2026-11-19T14:55:29.443Z","windowHours":48,"entries":[{"rank":1,"story":{"publicId":"7d0e1236-abef-423d-902f-c20addadebc1","title":"巴西两研究揭示过度训练致小鼠多巴胺异常升高及潜在健康风险"},"heat":15.6,"trend":"up","trendPct":116.7,"badges":["rising"],"participantCount":2,"sourceCount":2,"sourceNames":["奇客 Solidot","ScienceDaily 健康医学"],"participants":[{"iconUrl":"/hot-pages/acadhot/data/media/77c233158f61553b453a41a55928d5b940f130bdea86733b1c752d8dbb5a7edc.webp","iconSrcSet":"/hot-pages/acadhot/data/media/985e5904e488a8ecc8ea512b301064cad09ee3a3e2ca70b75fc6b8242fe53875.webp 48w, /hot-pages/acadhot/data/media/77c233158f61553b453a41a55928d5b940f130bdea86733b1c752d8dbb5a7edc.webp 96w","name":"奇客 Solidot","kind":"editorial"},{"iconUrl":"/hot-pages/acadhot/data/media/bc515405eef0819dba7953a740e698c1e3de3324241b33997d38f154c3d3aa55.webp","iconSrcSet":"/hot-pages/acadhot/data/media/161ccbabfd58db0dfa44e16247e623a9c9b24eb5a0b82234f28ae315171f66be.webp 48w, /hot-pages/acadhot/data/media/bc515405eef0819dba7953a740e698c1e3de3324241b33997d38f154c3d3aa55.webp 96w","name":"ScienceDaily 健康医学","kind":"editorial"}],"spark":[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,6.6,6.4,6.2],"summary":"巴西里贝朗普雷托体育教育学校（EEFERP-USP）团队在《Neuroscience》发表研究，通过单次高强度运动和八周渐进式过度训练两组小鼠实验，发现后者纹状体多巴胺浓度在运动后48小时持续升高32%（p<0.01），酪氨酸羟化酶（TyrH）活性同步下降18%（样本量n=60，检测方法为HPLC-MS和化学发光法）。该团队后续通过圣保罗大学合作研究（未注明期刊）发现，长时间高强度运动同样导致小鼠海马体内多巴胺水平异常偏高，并可能引发失眠、焦虑和持续性疲劳，但未提供具体样本量及检测方法。运动医学界对‘过度训练’的界定标准存在分歧，部分学者认为需结合心率变异性和皮质醇水平综合评估。","latest":"过度运动扰乱多巴胺调节机制","cover":null}]}